  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Reynolds number is given by,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#961;</mi><mi>v</mi><mi>d</mi></mrow><mi>&#951;</mi></mfrac></math>, where,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo></math>flow velocity,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo></math>hydraulic diameter of the pipe,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#961;</mi><mo>=</mo></math>density of the fluid &amp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#951;</mi><mo>=</mo></math>coefficient of viscosity of the fluid.</p><p>Reynolds number is the ratio of inertial forces to viscous forces within a fluid which is subjected to relative internal movement due to different fluid velocities.</p>",
